rapies. The collaboration between healthcare providers and caregivers is essential for optimizing patient outcomes and enhancing the quality of life for individuals relying on home nutrition [Data: Reports (558); Entities (16328); Relationships (14333)].\n\n## Research contributions to nutritional practices\n\nResearch efforts, particularly those led by prominent figures like Bozzetti F and De Cos Blanco AI, have significantly advanced the field of home artificial nutrition. Their contributions include developing guidelines and conducting studies that inform best practices in nutritional support for patients, especially those with complex medical needs such as cancer. This research is critical for improving patient care and ensuring that nutritional interventions are effective and evidence-based [Data: Reports (558); Entities (12539, 16325); Relationships (19183, 20552)].", "# Ketogenic Diet and Epilepsy Management Community\n\nThe community focuses on the ketogenic diet as a therapeutic approach for managing refractory epilepsy, particularly in children. Key entities include the ketogenic diet itself, various types of seizures, and associated complications, highlighting the interconnectedness of dietary management and seizure control.\n\n## Efficacy of the ketogenic diet in seizure management\n\nThe ketogenic diet is primarily utilized to manage seizures in patients with refractory epilepsy, providing an alternative treatment option when conventional medications fail. This dietary approach has shown significant efficacy in reducing the frequency and severity of seizures, particularly in children and adolescents. The diet's mechanism involves a high-fat, low-carbohydrate intake that alters the brain's energy metabolism, making it a valuable therapeutic strategy for individuals suffering from intractable epilepsy. Research indicates that the diet can be particularly beneficial for patients with conditions like Lennox-Gastaut syndrome and tuberous sclerosis, which are